course: dictionary
lesson: 15945
title: Unsigned
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unsigned is made of un-, which means not, and signed, which means it has a name or signature on it. So unsigned means there is no name written on it. «The note was unsigned, so nobody knew who had written it.» The words around it give the clue: nobody knew who wrote it.
explain: Always check the words around the word. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The note had no name on it, so nobody knew who had written it» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Unsigned also has meanings in music and maths. «An unsigned band» has no contract with a record company. «An unsigned number» has no plus or minus sign and is never negative. The subject tells you which meaning to use: music, sport, or maths.
fact: Unsigned means not signed, with no name written on it.
fact: «An unsigned letter» is anonymous: you do not know who wrote it.
fact: A permission slip that is unsigned is not allowed until a parent signs it.
fact: In sport or music, unsigned means not having a contract with a team or a record company.
fact: In computing, an unsigned whole number can only be 0 or positive.
exercise: «The birthday card was unsigned, so Mia did not know who had sent it.» What does unsigned mean here? | Written in pencil | Sent by post on a Monday | *There was no name written on it | Very large and bright
exercise: A maths book says, «An unsigned number has no plus or minus sign.» What does this tell you? | *It is never negative | It must be written in words | It is always negative | It is always a fraction
exercise: «The band was unsigned, so it had no contract with a record company.» What does unsigned mean for a band? | Famous all over the world | Signed up with lots of fans | Lost in a music shop | *Not signed to a record company
test: «The permission slip was unsigned, so Sam could not go on the trip.» Why could Sam not go? | The bus was full | Sam had lost his shoes | *No parent had signed the slip | The trip was cancelled because of rain
test: In computing, an unsigned whole number can only be what? | Negative | A word | A fraction | *0 or positive
exam: Why would a teacher say an unsigned permission slip is not enough? | Because the teacher lost her pen | Because the slip is too long to read | Because the slip is the wrong colour | *Because the trip is not allowed until a parent signs
